{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p4-acbc0afb","text":"No layout.js? Let's check app directory.

The failure: next/font/google fetches fonts from Google at build time; the loader failing with "Cannot read properties of null (reading '1')" is a known issue when the font fetch returns an error (offline/no network, or version mismatch). Since this machine may have no internet access to fonts.googleapis.com... Actually it did `npm install lucide-react` fine, so network exists. Hmm.

Known cause: `IBM_Plex_Sans` with weight list — in newer Next versions, variable fonts... The error at loader.js:112 reading [1] of null is typically the CSS parse of the font file URLs. Possibly Google Fonts returned a CSS response the parser couldn't handle, or the request was blocked.

Better fix per instruction: don't guess. But a robust fix used commonly: `display: 'swap'` fine. Alternative: use `next/font/local` or remove next/font. But how many pages? 5 pages each declare their own font — that's odd (no layout.js?). Let's look at app dir structure and one page's font usage.","open":false,"collapse":"preview"}
